WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.701
-Our next guest is an
Emmy-nominated actress

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.801
and comedian you know
from shows such as "Barry,"

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:06.667
"The Good Place"
and "A League of Their Own."

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:09.167
She stars in "Shotgun Wedding,"
which is streaming now

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:10.367
on Prime Video.

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:11.734
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:12.968
-Peek-a-boo.
-Oh.

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.133
-Hi.

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:16.133
[ Smooching ]

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:23.601
Oh, Darcy, I am so honored
to bare witness to this sacred

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:27.234
observance of rebirth
and devotion.

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:28.267
-Same.

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:32.000
-Thank you.
[ Chuckles ]

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.400
Renata.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.767
♪♪

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:39.400
-I need to go
to the ladies room.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.367
-Please welcome back to the
show, our friend

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:43.267
D'Arcy Carden, everybody!

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:45.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:53.734
♪♪

00:00:53.734 --> 00:01:02.801
♪♪

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.200
Welcome back.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.300
-Thanks for having me.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.567
-It's very lovely
to have you here.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.968
it's very lovely to have
you back in New York City.

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.367
You lived here for a long time.
-I did.

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:14.567
-Now you and your husband
live in L.A.,

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:15.667
and now you're both back.

00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:17.033
Are you going to enjoy
your time here?

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:18.667
-We are. We're going to stay
here for a few extra days.

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.501
-Okay.
-We're going to see some shows.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:23.968
I'm really excited about
seeing any old musical.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:26.067
-Are you pro musical?
-I'm way pro musical.

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:27.534
-How is your husband, Jason,
with musicals?

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:28.868
-Less.
-Okay. Yeah.

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.334
-Yeah.
-But that's okay.

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:31.667
-Yeah.
-He's a very supportive husband.

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:33.267
He goes to them?
-Yeah, he'll do it. He'll do it.

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:36.000
He wants to see something where,
like, our souls are ripped out

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.434
and we're like crying
and we learn something.

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:40.234
-Oh, yeah. Boo.
-I know, it's boring.

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:41.701
-Go learn something
on your own time.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.033
-That's what I say
from the audience.

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:44.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:45.834
And they're like,
"Get out of here.

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:49.434
-This is very exciting,
you filmed season 4 of "Barry,"

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:50.901
which is a show
I love a great deal.

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:53.300
-Yeah.
-And obviously, close to a lot

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.734
of people in this cast,
gotten to know

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:56.334
Henry Winkler a little bit.

00:01:56.334 --> 00:02:00.334
And I'm happy to say my
interactions with him,

00:02:00.334 --> 00:02:03.000
he does come off as the nicest
human being in the world.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.701
-It's really genuine.
-You worked with him even more.

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:05.767
-Yeah.

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:07.000
-Have you seen this
to be the case.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.200
-I have seen this
to be the case.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.167
-Okay.
-He's like -- he's like

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:12.100
the best person in the world.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.767
An example would be
I ran into him

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.133
and his lovely wife Stacey
recently,

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:20.267
and I was complaining to them
that my husband --

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:22.634
we just talked About him --
-Yeah.

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:24.400
This is a very big segment
for him so far.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:27.934
-He was going out of town,
and I was going to be

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:30.400
so scared to be in our house
by myself.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.434
And they both were like,
"Well, you'll stay with us.

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:34.667
You'll stay -- you will stay
with us.

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:36.367
You'll in our extra room and you
will stay with us.

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:37.968
And what you're going to do
is stay with us."

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:39.834
It was like there was no --
there was no conversation.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:41.000
-Did you hesitate?

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.934
-I was like, oh,
they're going to say it

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:43.934
and they don't mean it.

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:46.200
There was follow-up texts.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:51.067
♪ It was the best weekend
of my life ♪

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:52.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:53.167
-Were they great hosts?

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:54.767
-The best hosts!
-Oh, my God.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:56.100
-I had my own room.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.701
They had a little toothbrush,
little like face wash.

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:00.801
Henry had, like, put on the
right channel,

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:02.968
like on the TV,
a music channel.

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:05.067
They are the best.

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:06.567
I mean, like,
Henry made me breakfast.

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:08.100
I'm not kidding.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.100
They're the best people
in the world.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.334
I love them.
They're dear to me.

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:14.133
-It would have been such a
bummer if they had

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:15.234
murdered you, just because.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.601
-Yeah, I guess you're right.
-'Cause a lot of those things

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:21.834
are also what people
that would murder you would do.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:24.901
Like, they'd put out the
toothbrush to put you at ease.

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:26.100
-Totally.
-You're like, if you were going

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.200
to murder me you wouldn't
put out a toothbrush.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.234
-He would never put out
a toothbrush.

00:03:28.234 --> 00:03:29.534
And then,
in the middle of the night,

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:31.000
just absolute murder.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.367
-Yeah.
-No, it was the best.

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:34.367
-They're like, "Are your teeth
nice and clean?"

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:36.400
-"They have to be clean."
-"They have to be clean."

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.200
This is a fantastic cast.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.734
We only saw a couple of people
from the clip,

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:44.634
but a lot of you who filmed
this movie, "Shotgun Wedding,"

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:48.033
got to live together
in a beautiful resort home?

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:50.601
-I know. We keep saying home,
but it is the most --

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:53.868
it's like a, you know,
17-room house.

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:56.467
It is a mansion on the beach.
-Yeah.

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:59.300
-That is a wonderful, kind of,
job to get in show business.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.634
-It's almost not a job.
-Yeah.

00:04:01.634 --> 00:04:03.767
And so, you got to live
with, like, Cheech Marin.

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:05.100
-Yep.
-Who was in that clip.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.801
-Yeah, that I kissed.
-Yeah, you kissed Cheech Marin

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:09.601
multiple times
in that clip alone.

00:04:09.601 --> 00:04:11.334
I can only imagine how much more
kissing happens

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:12.901
in the rest of the movie.
-You gotta check it out.

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:15.200
I literally never do it again.
-And also, Jennifer Coolidge,

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.934
who I guess only does
resort work now.

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:18.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.834 --> 00:04:20.534
-She's a smart woman.
-She's a very smart woman.

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:23.067
-She's like, vacation, get paid.

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:25.234
-I thrive in that environment.
-I know.

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:26.734
How was -- what was your
first meeting

00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:28.400
with Jennifer Coolidge like?
-Oh, God.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:29.767
It was great, actually.

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:33.934
She -- I was eating breakfast
at the hotel

00:04:33.934 --> 00:04:35.267
before we moved
to the big mansion.

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:37.234
I was eating breakfast
at the hotel and I see her

00:04:37.234 --> 00:04:39.667
come in and sit down, and I was
so excited to see her.

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:41.400
And she, at one point, turns
around and she looks at me

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.567
and she goes, "Hey, I know you."

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:44.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:46.200
And I was like, "Hi."

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:47.601
And she's like,
"We just worked together."

00:04:47.601 --> 00:04:49.968
And I was like, "No.
No, we didn't --

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:51.367
no, we didn't work together."

00:04:51.367 --> 00:04:54.267
And she's like, "Yeah, yeah.
we just worked together, right?"

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:57.400
And I was like, "Jennifer,
I don't know how to say this,

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.367
if we worked together,
I would know because

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:01.467
I'm obsessed with you.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.267
I love you," and she got it.

00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:04.534
-Yeah.
-She's like, "Oh, yeah."

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:05.667
-It's funny.

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.400
I've had that a few times
where people who

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.367
are way more famous than me...
-I know, I know.

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:11.300
-...insist we met before,
and I have to be like,

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:14.267
"Don't take this the wrong way,
I'd [bleep] remember."

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:15.467
Yeah.
-That's it.

00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:16.501
-Yeah.
-That's it.

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:17.934
You're like, you can't --

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:19.667
you have to just say it bluntly.

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:21.534
You're like, "Trust me!

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:23.367
I would have told
my family about this."

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:25.300
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.000
-I have more to ask you
about the film.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.767
We'll be right back with
our friend, D'Arcy Carden.

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:30.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

